   "args": {
    "summary": "Root cause: the instance layer held girder.count_per_span = 4 while the description states 3 precast small box girders per span. The rule MR-02 (girder.A/I = A_single·n_girders) reused this stale count in the model-check layer, so the sparse girder self-weight was 4/3 of the correct value and L3-1/L3-2/L3-3 (reaction sum = total self-weight, w = γA, frequency range) failed. The accepted decisions themselves had been computed with n_girders = 3, so they were correct; only the instance field was wrong.\n\nRepair: corrected girder.count_per_span to 3 with write_instance. Re-verified all girder quantities. The full model was regenerated and all L1 (topology), L2 (code/consistency) and L3 (mechanics) checks now pass.\n\nFinal model: 2D spine-beam idealization of a single simply supported 30 m span; 3 precast prestressed small box girders merged into one equivalent beam (A = 3.417 m², I = 1.065 m⁴, Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 88.84 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m). Supports 0 and 1 are abutments on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400 mm, 5 layers × 8 mm, Ge = 1.0 MPa), 6 bearings per line (2 per girder end), modelled as vertical springs (Kv = 8.518×10⁶ kN/m, S = 10.71) with longitudinal springs (Kh = 18 000 kN/m) and free rotation. Live load: Highway Class II, 2 design lanes, carriageway 9 m; qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk(30 m) = 240 kN, impact factor μ = 0.201 (from f1 = 3.40 Hz per JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nKey results: first three vertical frequencies 3.40 / 13.49 / 29.88 Hz; self-weight reactions 1332.5 kN per abutment (sum 2665.1 kN = w·L); self-weight midspan moment 9994 kN·m; live-load max positive moment 6450 kN·m."
   },
